      "caption": {
        "html": "Biosynthetic route previously thought to lead to psilocybin. It has recently been shown that 4-hydroxylation and O-phosphorylation immediately follow decarboxylation, and neither dimethyltryptamine nor psilocin are intermediates, although spontaneously generated psilocin can be converted back to psilocybin.<sup about=\"#mwt1440\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Fricke2017_309-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Fricke2017&quot;}}\"><a href=\"./Psilocybin#cite_note-Fricke2017-309\" id=\"mwD_0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD_4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD_8\">[</span>305<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwEAA\">]</span></span></a></sup>",
